2.0.1:

  -- New Features --

[New] Pressure-to-response scoring model: exponential-decay scoring replaces
      fixed count thresholds; events add weighted pressure per rule, pressure
      decays via configurable half-life, bans fire when accumulated pressure
      exceeds trip point; cross-service aggregate trip; all math in native awk
      floats; old TRIG/TRIG_WINDOW configs auto-migrate via importconf
[New] Per-rule pressure configuration via pressure.conf: PRESSURE_WEIGHT,
      PRESSURE_TRIP, SKIP_ALERT, RULE_EMAIL with three-tier precedence
      (rule file > pressure.conf > conf.bfd); pressure trip ceiling enforced
      at 200 with importconf clamping
[New] Country pressure multipliers: auto-enabled when pressure-country.conf
      has entries; IP-to-country lookup via ipcountry.dat binary search
[New] FIREWALL="auto" with 8 backends: APF, CSF, firewalld, UFW, nftables,
      iptables, route, custom; auto-detection in priority order; nftables
      sets, iptables chain, firewalld rich rules, route blackhole
[New] Full IPv6 support: dual-stack detection, banning, and local address
      exclusion; BAN_COMMAND_V6/UNBAN_COMMAND_V6 for firewalls requiring
      separate commands
[New] Temporary bans with auto-expiry (BAN_TTL); recidivism escalation
      (BAN_ESCALATE_AFTER/BAN_ESCALATE_WINDOW); escalation modes
      (none/linear/double with configurable cap); retry with exponential
      backoff; old names (BAN_DURATION, BAN_PERMANENT_AFTER/WINDOW) accepted
[New] Distributed attack detection: SUBNET_TRIG unique IPs from same subnet
      triggers subnet ban; configurable IPv4/IPv6 masks
[New] Watch mode (-w/--watch): continuous daemon with configurable interval;
      SIGHUP config reload; systemd unit and SysVinit init script; dead-PID
      lock recovery for cron fallback
[New] Scan mode (--scan): full-log processing for all rules or a specific
      rule; supports dry-run, --max-lines=N, --scan-timeout=N
[New] Multi-channel alerting: email (text/HTML/multipart with SMTP relay
      support), Slack (webhook and Bot API), Telegram (Bot API), and Discord
      (webhook); configurable per-channel in conf.bfd; --test-alert for all
      channels; digest mode with configurable interval and spool flush
[New] Alert rendering pipeline: customizable {{VAR}} template partials
      (files/alert/) for email and messaging; inline CSS HTML with severity
      colors, pressure bar, country flags, reputation links (AbuseIPDB,
      Shodan, VirusTotal, IPinfo, GreyNoise); safe awk ENVIRON substitution
[New] Template overrides: alert/custom.d/ directory for per-file template
      customization that persists across upgrades; auto-migration of
      previously modified templates; health check reports active overrides
[New] Declarative rule engine with fail2ban-compatible <HOST> patterns,
      dual IPv4/IPv6 boundary-aware regex, and IGNOREREGEX per-rule exclusion
[New] 37 new service rules (57 total): apache-auth, nginx-http-auth,
      mysqld-auth, wordpress, webmin, directadmin, cyrus-imap, roundcube,
      plesk, dropbear, http_401, pam_generic, named, postgresql, openvpn,
      phpmyadmin, gitlab, grafana, proxmox, lighttpd, mongodb, xrdp, cpanel,
      interworx, gitea, nextcloud, cockpit, postscreen, vaultwarden,
      guacamole, haproxy, squid, sogo, freeswitch, ejabberd, drupal,
      jellyfin, powerdns
[New] Existing rule expansions: sshd (3 to 12 patterns), dovecot (2 to 6
      with ManageSieve), postfix (connection-abuse and postscreen patterns),
      proftpd (1 to 4), exim (Debian support), asterisk (SecurityEvent),
      sendmail (AUTH failure), mongodb (JSON structured log), apache-auth
      (digest auth)
[New] Systemd journal reader with transparent fallback (36 of 57 rules);
      LOG_SOURCE config (auto/file/journal); cursor-based journal tracking;
      36 service-to-journalctl filter mappings via dynamic registry
[New] Events CLI (-e/--events): active event dashboard showing all tracked
      IPs with pressure scores, event counts, services, and ban proximity;
      per-IP detail with failure counts and log sample; CIDR subnet reports;
      attack.pool-backed durable event history; --sort=count|time|ip,
      --24h/--7d/--30d time window filters
[New] Threat activity report (-a/--activity): summary header with aggregate
      unique IPs and total counts (24h/7d), active bans, per-service
      dual-interval breakdown with top country; IP search integration;
      --attackpool retained as silent alias
[New] Structured output (--json/--csv) for ban list (-l), events (-e),
      and threat activity (-a) including per-service breakdowns
[New] CLI expanded from 4 to 21 flags: -S/--status, -C/--config, -R/--rules,
      -T/--test, --test-pattern, -l/--list, -u/--unban, -b/--ban, -c/--check,
      -d/--dryrun, -w/--watch, -V/--verbose, -v/--version, -h/--help,
      --flush-temp, --flush-all, --json, --csv, --test-alert, --scan,
      -e/--events, -a/--activity
[New] Health check (-c/--check): validates config, log paths, firewall
      binaries, rule status, state directories, tlog cursors, active bans,
      messaging channel config, and alert template presence
[New] Verbose mode (-V/--verbose): per-IP pressure score, trip threshold,
      effective weight, and country multiplier shown during detection cycles
[New] LOG_IDLE_SUPPRESS config variable (default: 1) suppresses idle
      zero-event run-complete messages from syslog
[New] FAIL_COUNT template variable: actual failure count passed through
      alert pipeline; shown alongside pressure score in all alert channels
[New] tlog_lib.sh shared incremental log reader: atomic cursor writes,
      optional flock-based locking, cursor validation with auto-reset, stale
      cursor protection, multi-format compressed rotation support, and
      copytruncate handling
[New] elog_lib.sh structured logging library: severity levels, classic
      syslog-style and JSON output formats, structured JSONL audit events
      for block_added/block_removed/config_loaded/config_error/service_state
[New] alert_lib.sh shared alert library: template engine, MIME builder,
      email delivery (local MTA and SMTP relay), digest/spool management,
      multi-channel dispatch (Slack, Telegram, Discord)
[New] pkg_lib.sh v1.0.2 shared packaging library: standardized backup,
      file operations, service lifecycle, cron management, man page and
      bash completion install, and uninstall primitives
[New] bfd.1 nroff man page: OPTIONS, CONFIGURATION, PRESSURE MODEL,
      FIREWALL, RULES, FILES, SIGNALS, EXIT CODES sections
[New] bfd.bash-completion: context-sensitive tab completion for all CLI
      flags, IPs, rule names, config variables, and file paths
[New] importconf rewritten: awk-based config merge preserving user values;
      TRIG to PRESSURE_TRIP migration; thresholds.conf to pressure.conf
      per-rule translation; events.dat to pressure.dat migration;
      pre-2.0.1 backward compat
[New] install.sh: custom paths via INSTALL_PATH/BIN_PATH env vars; man
      page, bash completion, SysVinit init script installation; auto-enable
      watch mode on fresh install; upgrade detection via pkg_lib
[New] uninstall.sh: root check; service stop ordering; man page, completion,
      init script, backup directory, and custom log path cleanup
[New] Security functions: safe_source() validates ownership and permissions
      before sourcing; strict IP and email validation; rule name sanitization
[New] RPM packaging: FHS-compliant layout (/usr/sbin, /usr/lib/bfd,
      /etc/bfd, /usr/share/bfd, /var/lib/bfd); symlink farm for backward
      compat; config(noreplace); single spec covers el7/el8/el9/el10
[New] DEB packaging: FHS layout with dh_link-based symlink farm;
      debhelper-compat 13; conffile protection; single .deb covers Debian 12
      and Ubuntu 18/20/22/24
[New] GitHub Actions CI pipeline: 10-OS Docker matrix with Buildx caching,
      bash -n syntax checks, and shellcheck static analysis
[New] GitHub Actions release workflow: builds RPM and DEB packages in
      parallel on tag push; creates GitHub Release with assets
[New] BATS test suite: 1200 tests across 36 files with parallel runner
      and 10 Dockerfiles
[New] UAT scenario test suite: 66 tests across 10 categories covering
      ban lifecycle, escalation, detection pressure, scan mode, config
      health, ignore lists, investigation, watch mode, CLI UX, output quality
[New] UAT scenario expansion: 4 new test files (20 tests) covering
      multi-service detection, error paths, alert template validation,
      and concurrent operations; new helpers for service-specific log
      injection, alert capture, and state corruption

  -- Bug Fixes --

[Fix] Security: alert eval echo injection replaced with safe template
      expansion; show_config() eval injection guarded by whitelist;
      BAN_COMMAND template extracted raw preventing premature expansion;
      reject group-writable files in safety checks; sanitize credentials
      in alert log excerpts; validate IGNOREREGEX patterns before use
[Fix] Security: safe_source() applied to all sourced files; state file
      operations wrapped in flock; mktemp replaces PID-based temp files;
      tlog gunzip/gzip race replaced with zcat
[Fix] Global lock: FD-based flock replaced with mkdir-based lock eliminating
      eval and fd-0-close risk; PID liveness check clears dead holder
      immediately for cron recovery
[Fix] Watch mode: SIGTERM/SIGINT now properly exit the daemon; config
      reload unsets vars before re-sourcing to prevent stale values; clears
      pressure arrays; re-registers journal filters on SIGHUP; validation
      uses return instead of exit to prevent daemon crash; suppress elog
      stdout in daemon mode to prevent duplicate syslog entries
[Fix] HTML email: base64-encode HTML MIME part to comply with RFC 5321
      998-character line limit; fixes Exim rejection of long inline-CSS lines
[Fix] SMTP relay: TLS conditional on URL scheme (smtps:// and smtp://:587
      require TLS, smtp://:25 is plain); credentials optional for auth-free
      internal relays; curl stderr captured for error reporting
[Fix] Upgrade path: importconf preserves pressure-country.conf, custom rule
      files, exclude.files, custom alert templates, tlog cursor state files,
      and user-customized cron schedule; validates UNBAN_COMMAND binaries;
      merge_conf() preserves original file permissions after awk rewrite
[Fix] install.sh: stop watch mode before upgrade; systemd unit sed uses
      auto-detected unit directory; legacy /etc/systemd/system/ units cleaned
      on upgrade; PKG_BACKUP_SYMLINK set for correct importconf path
      resolution; BINPATH parent dir creation; sourced libraries set to 640
[Fix] uninstall.sh: backup glob widened to match both old (.bk.*) and new
      pkg_lib (.TIMESTAMP) naming formats
[Fix] nftables status: count actual set elements instead of reporting 1
[Fix] cron.daily: use dedicated lock file for flock to avoid write
      contention; check mkdir-based lock before rotating state files
[Fix] JSON escape: newline, tab, CR, backspace, and formfeed per RFC 8259
[Fix] Attack pool dedup: exact matching for rule names prevents false
      deduplication of similar service names (vsftpd/vsftpd2)
[Fix] Config validation: added OUTPUT_SYSLOG, EMAIL_ADDRESS, BFD_LOG_PATH,
      BAN_RETRY_COUNT, EMAIL_LOGLINES, LOG_FORMAT, LOG_LEVEL, and
      SCAN_TIMEOUT=0 validation
[Fix] Rule variable leakage: IGNOREREGEX/PORTS/SKIP_ALERT/RULE_EMAIL now
      properly reset between rules via save/restore/clear helpers
[Fix] CLI exit codes: all dispatch branches validate args and propagate
      correctly; suppress version banner for --json/--csv structured output
[Fix] Firewall backends: hardcoded paths replaced with command -v discovery;
      CIDR addresses pass through without extra suffix; guard against empty
      ip6tables binary with warning
[Fix] Symlink handling: stat -c calls add -L flag to dereference symlinks
      for package installs where files are symlinks to FHS locations
[Fix] Quiet mode (-q): remove stderr redirect so genuine errors reach
      cron's mail handler; stdout suppression sufficient for cron silence
[Fix] tlog: log rotation duplicate output; BASERUN install-time path
      replacement; unquote journal filter for multi-filter entries
[Fix] State files: restore 600 permissions after awk rewrite temp file;
      enforce 750 on tmp/ and stats/ directories; log file chmod 640
[Fix] Pressure alerts: format_alert_body field count corrected;
      ATTACK_COUNT backward compat uses pressure/1000 for old templates
[Fix] Display: status rounding normalized to match pressure computation;
      hardcoded trip defaults corrected from 15 to 20
[Fix] Ignore files: inline comments after IPs now handled correctly
[Fix] Subnet detection: defensive guard for masks below /8
[Fix] Rule fixes: postgresql path test, vsftpd2 tag collision, modsec
      variable rename, missing SKIP_ALERT in postfix/proftpd, ignore.hosts
      missing ::1 loopback
[Fix] IPv6: grep false-match replaced with exact matching
[Fix] Journal: filter key mismatch for rh_ipop3d; dispatch bypassed
      existing log files
[Fix] Packaging: tlog_lib.sh and elog_lib.sh added to RPM spec and DEB
      manifests; SysVinit service stop and deregister in all scriptlets
[Fix] Miscellaneous: POSIX == to = in test brackets; sed -r to sed -E;
      WATCH_INTERVAL default syntax; UNBAN_COMMAND warning gated on
      FIREWALL="custom"; firewalld examples removed --permanent flag
[Fix] haproxy rule: remove redundant inline KERNEL_LOG_PATH default to match
      convention used by all other rules referencing KERNEL_LOG_PATH

  -- Changes --

[Change] conf.bfd restructured into workflow-oriented sections (Pressure
      Model, Email Alerts, Banning, Custom Firewall Commands, Log Paths,
      Advanced); comments rewritten with worked examples; new variables
      documented as commented entries for discoverability
[Change] check() rewritten: pressure-based scoring replaces count-based
      thresholds; per-rule weight/trip/half-life; optional country
      multipliers; global cross-service pressure trip; per-cycle caching
      for country lookups and ignore lists; pre-computed IP occurrence counts
[Change] Alert subsystem refactored: legacy sourced-template approach
      replaced with shared alert_lib; BFD-specific rendering extracted to
      bfd_alert.sh; digest wrappers bridge BFD config to alert_lib API;
      SMTP_* variables mapped to shared ALERT_SMTP_* env vars
[Change] Internal libraries (bfd.lib.sh, tlog_lib.sh, elog_lib.sh,
      alert_lib.sh, internals.conf) moved to internals/ subdirectory
[Change] install.sh/uninstall.sh refactored to use pkg_lib functions for
      backup, file copy, permissions, symlinks, service management, cron,
      man page, and bash completion
[Change] Rule variables renamed for clarity: REQ to PREREQ, LP to LOG_FILE,
      TLOG_TF to LOG_TAG, ARG_VAL to MATCHED_HOSTS; backward-compat shim
      for custom rules using old names
[Change] Rule validation rewritten to distinguish inactive rules from
      genuine misconfigurations; detection output now verbose-only
[Change] Structured output refactor: shared data helpers for ban list,
      attack pool, events, and IP search; each format (text/JSON/CSV)
      shares a single data source
[Change] Logging: eout()/vout() rewritten as thin wrappers delegating to
      elog library; log calls assigned explicit severity levels; errors and
      warnings now write to stderr per UNIX convention; config_loaded audit
      event restricted to watch mode only
[Change] Attack pool enriched to 10-field format with country, action,
      duration, ports, pressure, and trip type; timestamp-based filtering
      replaces file-based archive rotation; age-based pruning with
      APOOL_RETENTION_DAYS (365) and APOOL_MAX_LINES (500000)
[Change] Rename EVENTS column/key to COUNT and "Events" labels to
      "Failures" across all text/JSON/CSV views for clarity
[Change] Events per-IP: append recent log activity section filtered by
      rule detection patterns; EMAIL_LOGLINES default reduced from 50 to 5
[Change] tlog_lib.sh updated to canonical 2.0.3: rotation refactored with
      pipe fallback for disk-full; journal flock support; cursor validation
      hardening
[Change] Email template HTML rebranded to rfxn.com design system with
      severity colors for ban types and pressure levels
[Change] postfix PORTS updated from 25,26 to 25,26,587,465
[Change] http_401 and pam_generic rules: conservative defaults to prevent
      false positives
[Change] UFW backend: comment marker on deny rules; graceful fallback for
      older versions
[Change] logrotate rewritten: copytruncate, weekly, compress, create 0640
[Change] cron.daily: flock-wrapped state rotation; copy-and-truncate
      preserves inodes; age-based pruning replaces daily rotation
[Change] Default cron interval reduced from 3 to 2 minutes
[Change] Shell modernization across all files: backticks to $(), $[expr]
      to $(( )), egrep to grep -E, for-cat to while-read, systematic
      variable quoting, hardcoded paths to command -v discovery
[Change] internals.conf: augment PATH with /sbin:/usr/sbin:/usr/local/bin
      to ensure binaries are discoverable under cron's minimal PATH
[Change] README wholesale rewrite: quick start, config reference, rule
      catalog, ban lifecycle, firewall backends, IPv6, CLI flags, scan mode,
      events dashboard, structured output, upgrade guide, troubleshooting
[Change] Version 1.6-1 to 2.0.1; copyright years updated to 2026
[Change] UAT watch mode tests: replace hardcoded sleep with batsman v1.2.0
      polling helpers (uat_wait_for_log, uat_wait_for_condition,
      uat_cleanup_processes); add uat_bfd_teardown_watch helper; add
      skip guard for timeout dependency
[Change] Documentation: update rule count (47 to 57) and rule catalog in
      man page and README; add proxy, messaging, and expanded service
      categories; update journal fallback ratio (36 of 57 rules)
[Change] Test renaming: rules-tier1/tier2 test files renumbered from
      40/41 to 42/43 to resolve conflict with events-list test files
[Change] UAT test quality: multi-service log injection moved to setup_file
      for test isolation; alert-validation BFD sourcing block extracted to
      _bfd_alert_render helper; hardcoded temp path replaced with mktemp;
      dead uat_bfd_setup_alert_capture helper removed
[Change] Jellyfin test cleanup moved from individual test bodies to teardown()
      so cleanup runs even when assertions fail
